    description: "Found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- jackson_dispatch.py: A class whose only Jackson hint is a field-level `@JsonProperty` is not a target, so its bean accessors get no edges -- evidence: the repro in notebook staleness_audit_10252026/verify/V07.md (`jackson edges: 0`).\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # a525
